{"title":"2014 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/5/c753ea984dbe33c78e96c210ee32bb8b99a4f1c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\dots,a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" /> be positive real numbers whose product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Show that the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b27963c145ad81900e7c98e3e3b3fcf0cbba997b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle\\frac{a_1}{1+a_1}+\\frac{a_2}{(1+a_1)(1+a_2)}+\\frac{a_3}{(1+a_1)(1+a_2)(1+a_3)}+\\cdots+\\frac{a_n}{(1+a_1)(1+a_2)\\cdots(1+a_n)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"495\" height=\"22\" /> is greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0788b2285e0b296fb58d7ed95e469decdd94f4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^n-1}{2^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"51\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d592a3f0abf59084984dfcdd0f1aab2d2ae853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_1}{1+a_1}+\\frac{a_2}{(1+a_1)(1+a_2)}+\\cdots+\\frac{a_n}{(1+a_1)(1+a_2)\\cdots (1+a_n)}\\\\=(1-\\frac{1}{1+a_1})+(\\frac{1}{1+a_1}-\\frac{1}{(1+a_1)(1+a_2)})+\\cdots+(\\frac{1}{(1+a_1)(1+a_2)\\cdots (1+a_{n-1})}-\\frac{1}{(1+a_1)(1+a_2)\\cdots (1+a_n)})\\\\=1-\\frac{1}{(1+a_1)(1+a_2)\\cdots (1+a_n)}\\\\\\geq 1-\\frac{1}{(2\\sqrt{1\\cdot a_1)}(2\\sqrt{1\\cdot a_2)}\\cdots (2\\sqrt{1\\cdot a_n)}}\\\\=1-\\frac{1}{2^n}\\\\=\\frac{2^n-1}{2^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"915\" height=\"244\" />\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234803\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 33/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 368/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1441/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.196      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    6.196      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17435:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234803 and revision id 205984. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}